page DocsServerCronJobs

title "CronJobs - Documentation"

template
<div class="min-h-[calc(100vh-4rem)] grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] bg-page transition-colors">

  <DocsSidebar active="server-cron" />

  <div class="min-w-0 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-10 py-6 sm:py-10">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">

    <article class="rounded-3xl border border-line bg-panel p-5 sm:p-8">
      <p class="text-zinc-500 text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] mb-3">Documentation / Inside a server</p>
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-light uppercase tracking-wide text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100">CronJobs</h1>
      <p class="text-zinc-500 text-sm mt-2 mb-8">The CronJobs page runs commands on a schedule. Open it with CronJobs in the menu on the left. Each job's output is added to its own log file on the server, so you can check what it did.</p>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-5">Creating a cron job</h2>

      <div class="space-y-7 mb-10">

        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500 text-white text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center">1</span>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <h3 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-base font-semibold">Start from a preset, or not</h3>
            <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1">The Laravel scheduler preset fills in a name, a schedule of every minute, and the command <span class="font-mono text-xs">php artisan schedule:run</span> inside an example site folder. Change the folder to your own site's, and you have what Laravel needs. You can also ignore the preset and fill everything in yourself.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500 text-white text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center">2</span>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <h3 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-base font-semibold">Name and command</h3>
            <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1">The name is for you, for example "Nightly cleanup". The command is what runs.</p>
            <div class="rounded-2xl border-l-2 border-l-brand-500 bg-brand-500/5 px-4 py-3 mt-3">
              <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">Cron has no working directory. When the command needs to run inside a folder, start it with <span class="font-mono text-xs">cd /path &amp;&amp;</span>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500 text-white text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center">3</span>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <h3 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-base font-semibold">Schedule</h3>
            <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1">Five fields: minute, hour, day of the month, month and day of the week. The default <span class="font-mono text-xs">* * * * *</span> means every minute. The buttons under the box fill it in for you:</p>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 mt-3">
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 mt-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500"></span><span><strong>Every minute</strong>, <strong>Every 5 min</strong>, <strong>Hourly</strong>, <strong>Nightly</strong> (midnight), <strong>Weekly</strong> (Sunday midnight) and <strong>Monthly</strong> (the 1st).</span></li>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 mt-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500"></span><span><strong>On reboot</strong>, which runs the command once each time the server starts.</span></li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-3">Times follow the server's timezone. You can change it in <a href="/docs/servers/settings-system" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">System and power</a>, so set it before you schedule anything.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500 text-white text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center">4</span>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <h3 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-base font-semibold">Run as user</h3>
            <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1">Pick the account on the server that runs the command. For a site's job, use that site's own user, so the files it creates belong to the right person. If the list of users cannot be read, an amber note says so and only the SSH user is offered.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
          <span class="w-7 h-7 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-brand-500 text-white text-xs font-semibold flex items-center justify-center">5</span>
          <div class="min-w-0">
            <h3 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-base font-semibold">Create cron job</h3>
            <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1">The job appears in the list below and starts running at its next scheduled time.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">Active cron jobs</h2>

      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">Each job is one card with its name, schedule, command and user. Before you have any, the card says "No cron jobs yet."</p>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden mb-8">

        <div class="px-5 py-4">
          <h3 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-semibold">Run now</h3>
          <p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1">Runs the command once, straight away, and shows what it printed under the card. If it printed nothing, you see "No output." A quick way to test a new job without waiting for its schedule.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="px-5 py-4 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <h3 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-semibold">Log</h3>
          <p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1">Shows the job's log file, where the output of every scheduled run is added. Select Log again to close it.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="px-5 py-4 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <h3 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-semibold">Delete</h3>
          <p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-1">Removes the job so it stops running. Select Delete, then Yes, delete it. Cancel backs out.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">When your account is locked</h2>

      <p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-8">If your account is locked for payment, Create cron job, Run now and Delete are greyed out and say "Pay to continue". You can still read logs.</p>

      <h2 class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">If something goes wrong</h2>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-line overflow-hidden">

        <div class="px-5 py-3.5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Couldn't create the cron job.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">A red message above the form. Read it. A schedule with the wrong number of fields, or an empty name or command, is the usual cause.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Couldn't run the command.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Shown under the job after Run now. The server could not run it. Check that it is online.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">The job runs but does nothing</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">Use Run now and read the output. A missing <span class="font-mono">cd /path &amp;&amp;</span> at the start of the command is the most common cause.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="px-5 py-3.5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
          <p class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 text-sm font-medium">Couldn't read the log. / Couldn't remove the cron job.</p>
          <p class="text-zinc-500 text-xs mt-0.5">The server did not answer. Check that it is online and try again.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 mt-8 pt-5 border-t border-stone-100 dark:border-white/5">
        <a href="/docs/servers/backups" class="text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">&larr; Backups</a>
        <a href="/docs/servers/workers" class="text-sm text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-500 hover:underline">Workers &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </article>

  </div>
  </div>
</div>